...because he didn't want sheldon to be embarrassed.

274
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,330
And there is nothing to be embarrassed about, okay?

275
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:59,790
Every family in america has a relative

276
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:02,990
Holed up in a garage somewhere huffing paint thinner.

277
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:04,600
No, I'm lost, too.

278
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,590
I think she skipped a step.

279
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:07,960
No, look.

280
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:10,210
Sheldon's cousin leo escaped rehab,

281
00:12:10,210 --> 00:12:11,800
And he's in a motel 8 in long beach.

282
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,060
The whole family's going out for an intervention.

283
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:15,790
Leonard is driving sheldon down there

284
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,630
To help him through this, because he's such a good man.

285
00:12:18,690 --> 00:12:21,090
Oh, another hug? thank you.

286
00:12:22,270 --> 00:12:23,860
All right, you guys, good luck.

287
00:12:23,930 --> 00:12:24,960
Thanks, penny.

288
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:26,160
Oh-- break a leg.

289
00:12:26,230 --> 00:12:28,260
Break a leg.

290
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,960
So, road trip to long beach.

291
00:12:30,030 --> 00:12:31,730
No. we're not going to long beach.

292
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:32,410
Why not?

293
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:33,960
Because sheldon doesn't have

294
00:12:34,030 --> 00:12:35,590
A drug-addicted cousin leopold.

295
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:37,630
Oh, too bad.

296
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,080
I've always wanted to go to long beach.

297
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,790
It's a very nice community.

298
00:12:41,790 --> 00:12:43,430
The queen mary is docked there.

299
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,510
Once the largest ocean liner in the world,

300
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,810
It's now a hotel and restaurant,

301
00:12:46,810 --> 00:12:48,630
Where they host a surprisingly gripping

302
00:12:48,690 --> 00:12:50,530
Murder mystery dinner.

303
00:12:50,590 --> 00:12:51,790
Sounds fun. I'm game.

304
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:52,790
Shotgun!

305
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,860
No, no, no.

306
00:12:54,930 --> 00:12:57,330
Leonard gets nauseous unless he sits in front,

307
00:12:57,390 --> 00:12:58,760
And even then, it's iffy.

308
00:13:00,090 --> 00:13:03,530
Wait, are we... really going to long beach?!

309
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:11,790
Leonard?

310
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,630
Leonard? leonard?

311
00:13:13,690 --> 00:13:15,230
Let it go, sheldon.

312
00:13:15,230 --> 00:13:16,480
The murderer was the first mate

313
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:19,030
Whether it makes sense to you or not.

314
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:21,890
No, that's the least of our worries.

315
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:24,190
I've been doing some research on addiction--

316
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,430
Both the biochemical and behavioral aspects--

317
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:27,500
And I think there's a problem

318
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,540
With the current version of our lie.

319
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:30,710
What are you talking about?

320
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:33,360
It's fine-- she bought it; it's over.

321
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:38,870
Sadly, it's not.

322
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:40,910
Substance abuse is a lifelong struggle,

323
00:13:40,910 --> 00:13:43,960
But beyond that, I have realized that the leo I described

324
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:45,550
Would not have agreed to go to rehab.

325
00:13:45,550 --> 00:13:47,360
Why not?

326
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:49,330
Because leo's a middle child.

327
00:13:49,390 --> 00:13:51,130
There is no leo!

328
00:13:51,190 --> 00:13:53,190
How can you say that?

329
00:13:56,390 --> 00:13:58,610
You didn't read the bio, did you?

330
00:13:59,290 --> 00:14:00,710
He's not just a middle child,

331
00:14:00,710 --> 00:14:02,350
He is the quintessential middle child--

332
00:14:02,350 --> 00:14:03,890
From a broken home, to boot.

333
00:14:03,890 --> 00:14:07,360
Psychologically speaking, the attention he gets by rebelling,

334
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,290
Even to the point of self-destruction,

335
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:11,860
Is more emotionally valuable than the help he would get at rehab.

336
00:14:11,930 --> 00:14:13,330
I've got a solution.

337
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:14,230
Great. what is it?

338
00:14:14,290 --> 00:14:16,760
Get out!

339
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,660
Fine.

340
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:26,250
I've hesitated to point this out,

341
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:28,030
But I must now remind you that we

342
00:14:28,090 --> 00:14:29,960
Are in our current predicament because of your initial

343
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:31,470
And totally inadequate deceit.

344
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:33,790
I'm just trying to clean up after your mess.

345
00:14:37,760 --> 00:14:39,510
We'll talk in the morning.

346
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:53,710
Morning.

347
00:14:54,410 --> 00:14:56,170
Who are you?

348
00:14:56,510 --> 00:14:59,020
I am sheldon's cousin leo.

349
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,030
Sheldon does not have a cousin leo.

350
00:15:06,090 --> 00:15:07,880
Au contraire.

351
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:09,440
I'm 26 years old.

352
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:13,130
I'm originally from... denton, texas,

353
00:15:13,190 --> 00:15:15,130
But I was a navy brat, so I was

354
00:15:15,190 --> 00:15:17,490
Brought up on a variety of military bases around the world.

355
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:20,180
As a result, I've often felt like an outsider--

356
00:15:20,180 --> 00:15:21,560
Never really fitting in,

357
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:24,930
Which is probably the reason for my substance abuse problem.

358
00:15:24,990 --> 00:15:27,360
Excuse me, we just went over this.

359
00:15:27,430 --> 00:15:29,900
As the quintessential middle child, your addiction

360
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:32,230
Is rooted in your unmet need for attention.

361
00:15:32,290 --> 00:15:35,330
Oh, sheldon, are we really going to go with pop psychology?

362
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,930
For your information, this is all based on solid research.

363
00:15:37,990 --> 00:15:40,630
Just stick with the character profile I wrote for you.

364
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:41,930
Sheldon? I'm sorry.

365
00:15:41,990 --> 00:15:44,370
Leonard, this is toby loobenfeld.

366
00:15:44,370 --> 00:15:45,700
He's a research assistant

367
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:47,130
In the particle physics lab,

368
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:50,520
But he also minored in theater at mit.

369
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:52,690
It was more of a double major, actually.

370
00:15:52,690 --> 00:15:54,000
Theater and physics.

371
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,990
You can guess which one my bourgeois parents

372
00:15:55,990 --> 00:15:56,830
Pushed me toward.

373
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:58,190
Yeah, I got it.

374
00:15:58,260 --> 00:16:00,290
Sheldon... why?

375
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:03,190
You see, while leo would not have gone into rehab,

376
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:06,090
It is completely plauible that we would have talked him

377
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:08,930
Into leaving the motel and coming home with us.

378
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:11,090
Oh... sheldon, how about this

379
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,260
As my motivation-- when I was 14 years old,

380
00:16:13,330 --> 00:16:17,830
I was abused in the philippines by a clubfooted navy chaplain.

381
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:21,160
No. we're going with middle child

382
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:25,050
And a genetic predisposition to inadequate serotonin production.

383
00:16:25,050 --> 00:16:28,550
Swell. how do I play genetic predisposition?

384
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,830
Subtextually, of course.

385
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:36,320
Just have fun with it.

386
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:42,330
Morning, penny.

387
00:16:42,390 --> 00:16:43,990
Hi. how did the intervention go?

388
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:47,430
Unfortunately, we weren't able to convince him to go to rehab.

389
00:16:47,430 --> 00:16:50,220
Oh. well, based on what you told me, I am not surprised.

390
00:16:52,670 --> 00:16:55,160
But we did convince him to leave the motel.

391
00:16:55,230 --> 00:16:56,730
Come say hello.

392
00:16:57,690 --> 00:17:01,560
Leo. this is penny,

393
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:02,730
Our friend and neighbor.

394
00:17:02,790 --> 00:17:04,290
Hi, leo.

395
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:06,190
How are you feeling?

396
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:13,190
Let me ask you something, penny.

397
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:15,960
Have you ever woken up in a fleabag motel

398
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:17,660
Covered in your own vomit,

399
00:17:17,730 --> 00:17:20,690
Next to a transsexual prostitute?

400
00:17:23,190 --> 00:17:24,690
No.

401
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:28,030
Then don't ask me how I'm feeling.

402
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:31,460
Well, that's leo.

403
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,530
Why don't you tell me about your showcase last night.

404
00:17:35,590 --> 00:17:36,960
Oh. it was okay, I guess.

405
00:17:37,030 --> 00:17:38,000
It wasn't a big turnout,

406
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,960
But they both really seemed to like it.

407
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,690
There were only two people there?

408
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,290
By the end, yeah.

409
00:17:44,870 --> 00:17:47,730
Damn you, chaplain harrigan!

410
00:17:49,530 --> 00:17:51,060
I'm... I'm sorry?

411
00:17:51,130 --> 00:17:52,930
The philippines.

412
00:17:54,810 --> 00:17:57,090
1992.

413
00:17:57,090 --> 00:17:59,120
The subic bay naval station.

414
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:02,330
A young boy on the cusp of manhood.

415
00:18:02,390 --> 00:18:04,530
His only companions,

416
00:18:04,590 --> 00:18:07,890
Mongrel dogs and malarial mosquitoes.

417
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,490
Desperate and alone,

418
00:18:09,490 --> 00:18:13,130
He reached out to a man who promised to introduce him

419
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:15,790
To a merciful, loving god,

420
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:17,790
But who instead introduced him

421
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:23,530
To a gin-pickled tongue shoved down his adolescent throat.

422
00:18:24,890 --> 00:18:26,960
What choice did he have but to drink,

423
00:18:27,030 --> 00:18:32,790
Shoot and snort his pain away?

424
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:35,370
Don't forget his genetic predisposition towards addiction.

425
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:37,330
That's never been proven. there have been studies.

426
00:18:37,390 --> 00:18:38,650
Not double-blind studies.

427
00:18:38,650 --> 00:18:40,110
How could there be a double-blind study?

428
00:18:40,110 --> 00:18:41,490
Who would be the control group?

429
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:43,700
As you can see, detoxing can get pretty ugly.

430
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:44,930
Let's give them some privacy.

431
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:46,260
Yeah.

432
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:47,960
Hey, do you want to come over to my place, have coffee?

433
00:18:48,030 --> 00:18:49,190
Oh, sounds good.

434
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:51,120
I have a video of me singing last night.

435
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,160
Do you want to see it?

436
00:18:53,190 --> 00:18:55,470
Gee, why wouldn't i?

437
00:18:55,470 --> 00:18:57,450
This is even better than you coming to the showcase,

438
00:18:57,450 --> 00:18:59,330
Because now I get to watch you watch me.

439
00:18:59,390 --> 00:19:01,090
Yeah...

440
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:04,270
Funny how things work out.

441
00:19:05,030 --> 00:19:06,330
...but he loved the companionship

442
00:19:06,390 --> 00:19:10,060
And the wisdom that his own father failed to provide.

443
00:19:10,990 --> 00:19:13,600
Your parents made the right decision.

444
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:21,230
I cannot work like this.

445
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:32,360
This is amazing.

446
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:36,020
Just sitting on a couch watching tv with a woman.

447
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:39,370
Not being drunk or, or high

448
00:19:39,370 --> 00:19:42,360
Or wondering if you're a dude down there.

449
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:47,790
Leo, you are a very sweet, really funny guy.

450
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:50,160
You're going to do okay.

451
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,440
One day at a time, penny.

452
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:57,880
One day at a time.

453
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:05,130
How long is he going to stay here?

454
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:07,060
He's a homeless drug addict, leonard.

455
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:09,020
Where is he going to go?

456
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:12,090
Boy, you have a lot to learn about lying.

